Hi everyone,

I am currently working on my master thesis
and I want to find out habitat preferences of my study species. I therefor
collected presence absence data of the species with wildlife cameras (20
cameras, 2 years, same location and dates) and footprint tunnels (100 tunnels,
1 year, 14 repetitions). Same parameters were collected on every camera (both
years) and footprint location. In addition, some more habitat parameters were
collected for the tunnels and in the second year of the cameras. The second
year of the cameras is the same time period as the data collection of the
tunnels.

I now have questions about the usage of the
functions colext() and occu().

First of all, I am analysing both datasets separately,
because I assume detection probability to be different among both methods, is
that correct?

Cameras:

1.
I am using function colext()
for multi-season occupancy models because I have data of two years. But two
seasons are not enough to calculate colonisation and extinction, as far as I
understood. Would it therefor make more sense to use as single season occupancy
model (function occu())? If so, how do I deal with different habitat parameters
and different values for parameters collected in both years? I was using colext()
to account for changes between the years.

2.
When using colext() for my
camera data I have two primary periods and 146 secondary periods (number of
days when cameras where operating). That seems quite a lot to me for the
secondary periods. Does it make the model worse if the number of primary
periods is that high?

Tunnels:

I tried both functions for tunnel data
(even though I only have one year) and for colext I created five primary
periods (one for every month). For both functions I get significant results for
some covariates, but they do differ between the functions. With colext function
I get lower AICs than with occu function. Should I therefor prefer the
multi-season framework for the tunnels?

Depending on your opinion I am also thinking
on creating more primary periods for cameras (1 month = 1 primary period), as I
also did for tunnels. Or would it be better to do the opposite and run single
season models which include both years?

I am very happy for every suggestions! Thanks
a lot in advance!

Hanna

